
  <sn><md>### **Rclone Cloud Storage Providers**


| **Provider**           | **Provider**        | **Provider**         | **Provider**       |
| ---------------------- | ------------------- | -------------------- | ------------------ |
| 1Fichier               | Akamai NetStorage   | Amazon S3            | Azure Blob Storage |
| Azure Files            | Backblaze B2        | Box                  | Cloudinary         |
| Digi Storage           | DigitalOcean Spaces | Drime                | Dropbox            |
| Enterprise File Fabric | FileLu              | Filen                | Files.com          |
| FTP                    | Gofile              | Google Cloud Storage | Google Drive       |
| Google Photos          | HDFS                | Hetzner Storage Box  | HiDrive            |
| HTTP                   | Huawei Drive        | iCloud Drive         | ImageKit           |
| Internet Archive       | Internxt            | Jottacloud           | Koofr              |
| Linkbox                | Mail.ru Cloud       | MEGA                 | Microsoft OneDrive |
| Oracle Object Storage  | OpenDrive           | OpenStack Swift      | pCloud             |
| PikPak                 | Pixeldrain          | premiumize.me        | Proton Drive       |
| put.io                 | QingStor            | Quatrix              | rsync.net          |
| Seafile                | SFTP                | Shade                | Sia                |
| SMB                    | Storj               | SugarSync            | Uloz.to            |
| WebDAV                 | Yandex Disk         | Zoho WorkDrive       | **—**              |

**Note:** Some entries such as **S3, Swift, WebDAV, SFTP, FTP, SMB, and HTTP** are protocols/backends rather than consumer cloud services themselves. They are nevertheless supported Rclone storage systems. ([Rclone][1])

For example, **Amazon S3-compatible providers** can include services such as AWS S3, Wasabi, Cloudflare R2, Backblaze B2, and DigitalOcean Spaces through the S3 backend. ([Rclone][2])

[Rclone — Supported Storage Systems](https://rclone.org/overview/?utm_source=chatgpt.com)

[1]: https://rclone.org/overview/?utm_source=chatgpt.com "Overview of cloud storage systems"
[2]: https://rclone.org/docs/?utm_source=chatgpt.com "Documentation"
</md></sn>
